{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'evidence_period|opens_as|why_a_separate_bet|settled_by' clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08 | head -80\"","aggregated_output":"clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/build_acceptance_judging.py:52:            'opens_as': t.get('opens_as'), 'settled_by': t.get('settled_by'), 'closest_open_thesis': t.get('closest_open_thesis'),\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/build_acceptance_judging.py:53:            'why_a_separate_bet': t.get('why_a_separate_bet')} for t in answer['new_theses'] if t['local_id'] in local]\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u1c-schema.json:21:     \"why_a_separate_bet\"\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u1c-schema.json:58:     \"why_a_separate_bet\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u1c-schema.json:80:     \"evidence_period\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u1c-schema.json:187:     \"evidence_period\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c3-schema.json:21:     \"why_a_separate_bet\"\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c3-schema.json:58:     \"why_a_separate_bet\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c3-schema.json:80:     \"evidence_period\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c3-schema.json:244:     \"evidence_period\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c17-schema.json:20:     \"opens_as\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c17-schema.json:21:     \"settled_by\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c17-schema.json:23:     \"why_a_separate_bet\"\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c17-schema.json:49:     \"opens_as\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c17-schema.json:59:     \"settled_by\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c17-schema.json:75:     \"why_a_separate_bet\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c17-schema.json:97:     \"evidence_period\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c17-schema.json:261:     \"evidence_period\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/acceptance-reader-settle-matters.md:13:2. A matter both readers list is kept (`settled_by: both`). Keep the better quote; it must be an exact span of the article.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/acceptance-reader-settle-matters.md:15:   keep it (`settled_by: third`) or drop it, with one short reason.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/acceptance-reader-settle-matters.md:22:                                \"quote\": \"<exact span>\", \"strength\": \"core|supporting\", \"settled_by\": \"both|third\", \"reason\": \"...\"}]},\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/acceptance-reader-settle-groups.md:24:{\"repeat_groups\": [{\"members\": [{\"matter\": \"<settled id>\", \"kind\": \"first|repeat|revision\"}], \"settled_by\": \"both|third\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/build_thesis_reading.py:45:                lines.append(f\"- {label} [{thesis.get('opens_as')}]: {thesis['description']} (period: {thesis.get('period')})\")\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c2-closing.txt:14:For each new thesis, check its closest_open_thesis and why_a_separate_bet: if the two answers cannot move apart, or the thesis falls under a 'do not open' item in section 3, drop the thesis and link its evidence to the open thesis.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c15o-closing.txt:15:For each new thesis, check its opens_as, settled_by, closest_open_thesis and why_a_separate_bet: drop the thesis if it fits none of the four reasons in section 3, if no public material will settle it on a date, if an open thesis exists and its answer cannot move apart from it, or if it falls under a 'do not open' item in section 3; then link its evidence to every open thesis it informs, or leave it without links.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c11-system.txt:122:- Before proposing a new thesis, name its reason (opens_as), the public material that will settle it (settled_by), and the closest\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c11-system.txt:170:- evidence_period: the period the reported fact, plan or forecast covers, as supported by the item; otherwise null. This is not the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10a-schema.json:20:     \"opens_as\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10a-schema.json:21:     \"settled_by\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10a-schema.json:23:     \"why_a_separate_bet\"\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10a-schema.json:49:     \"opens_as\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10a-schema.json:59:     \"settled_by\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10a-schema.json:75:     \"why_a_separate_bet\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10a-schema.json:97:     \"evidence_period\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10a-schema.json:261:     \"evidence_period\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u1-schema.json:21:     \"why_a_separate_bet\"\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u1-schema.json:58:     \"why_a_separate_bet\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u1-schema.json:80:     \"evidence_period\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u1-schema.json:187:     \"evidence_period\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/lfile-system.txt:158:- evidence_period: the period the reported fact, plan or forecast covers, as supported by the item; otherwise null. This is not the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u3-schema.json:21:     \"why_a_separate_bet\"\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u3-schema.json:58:     \"why_a_separate_bet\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u3-schema.json:80:     \"evidence_period\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u3-schema.json:204:     \"evidence_period\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:1344:- **Schema:** `opens_as` (an enum, checked by code) and `settled_by` (non-blank, checked by code) are required. The closing check\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:1903:**Theses** (each new or removed thesis read with its `why_a_separate_bet` and its article):\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:1961:- `why_a_separate_bet` aligned with the override;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:2765:- `opens_as` and `settled_by` are not in the library state, only in `trace.result`;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:2808:4. the reader table missed readers outside this path, and two old checks were not met (the quarterly rule, a blank `settled_by`);\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:2948:B's was unmeasured; the 18-month rule was stated for every obligation and checked on `opens_as`; a failure between the ladder write\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:2976:Version 11 carries these and the five answers (the request and the check share the `opens_as` scope; one commit a day before judging;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3125:14 matches in `settled_by` (\"quarterly earnings releases\"), 2 in `period`. Since D38 the judged question names its settling\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3241:| tables | \"the old quarterly check would refuse annual questions\" was a risk stated as a count | stated as a risk: the pattern matches `settled_by` in 14 of 34 and none of the seven fixture questions; Stage A reports the matches on real answers |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3998:*The object, from a field Step 1 already writes.* Over both runs, by the thesis's `opens_as`: product nodes and binding\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:4018:- *The object:* it refused a hard mapping from Step 1's `opens_as` to company or theme, with two stored counter-cases: a shared\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c15o-system.txt:122:- Before proposing a new thesis, name its reason (opens_as), the public material that will settle it (settled_by), and the closest\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c15o-system.txt:169:- evidence_period: the period the reported fact, plan or forecast covers, as supported by the item; otherwise null. This is not the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10b-schema.json:20:     \"opens_as\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10b-schema.json:21:     \"settled_by\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10b-schema.json:23:     \"why_a_separate_bet\"\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10b-schema.json:49:     \"opens_as\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10b-schema.json:59:     \"settled_by\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10b-schema.json:75:     \"why_a_separate_bet\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10b-schema.json:97:     \"evidence_period\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10b-schema.json:262:     \"evidence_period\": {\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/k6b-system.txt:156:- evidence_period: the period the reported fact, plan or forecast covers, as supported by the item; otherwise null. This is not the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/focused/focused_probe.py:34:        kinds.update({ids[t['local_id']]: t.get('opens_as') for t in answer['new_theses'] if t['local_id'] in ids})\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/focused/focused_probe.py:42:    new_kinds = {t['local_id']: t.get('opens_as') for t in answer['new_theses']}\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u1k-closing.txt:14:For each new thesis, check its closest_open_thesis and why_a_separate_bet: if the two answers cannot move apart, or the thesis falls under a 'do not open' item in section 3, drop the thesis and link its evidence to the open thesis.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10a-system.txt:122:- Before proposing a new thesis, name its reason (opens_as), the public material that will settle it (settled_by), and the closest\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c10a-system.txt:170:- evidence_period: the period the reported fact, plan or forecast covers, as supported by the item; otherwise null. This is not the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/acceptance-reader-settle.md:19:Return only JSON. `settled_by` is `both` when both readers listed the matter, or `third` when you decided it:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/acceptance-reader-settle.md:23:                                \"strength\": \"core|supporting\", \"settled_by\": \"both|third\", \"reason\": \"...\"}]},\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/acceptance-reader-settle.md:25: \"repeat_groups\": [{\"members\": [{\"matter\": \"...\", \"kind\": \"first|repeat|revision\"}], \"settled_by\": \"both|third\"}],\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c15yc-system.txt:122:- Before proposing a new thesis, name its reason (opens_as), the public material that will settle it (settled_by), and the closest\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c15yc-system.txt:169:- evidence_period: the period the reported fact, plan or forecast covers, as supported by the item; otherwise null. This is not the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c16-system.txt:122:- Before proposing a new thesis, name its reason (opens_as), the public material that will settle it (settled_by), and the closest\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c16-system.txt:185:- evidence_period: the period the reported fact, plan or forecast covers, as supported by the item; otherwise null. This is not the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c9-system.txt:126:- Before proposing a new thesis, name its reason (opens_as), the public material that will settle it (settled_by), and the closest\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c9-system.txt:177:- evidence_period: the period the reported fact, plan or forecast covers, as supported by the item; otherwise null. This is not the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c17-system.txt | sed -n '55,145p'; nl -ba clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c17-closing.txt | tail -8\"","aggregated_output":"    55\t  or consensus estimate) lists its useful figures in figures. Its results, guidance and estimates, margins included, inform an open thesis about its revenue or earnings\n    56\t  path when they bear on that path; a different period is not on its own a reason to leave them unlinked. When no open or new\n    57\t  thesis covers it, its links stay empty. A figure is useful when it can change what an analyst\n    58\t  expects of the company's revenue, profitability, funding or credit risk, or competitive position: a retailer's quarterly\n    59\t  same-store sales, an airline's guidance for next year's unit costs and analysts' consensus earnings for a bank are; a cash-rich\n    60\t  company's cash balance or cash flow usually changes none of these when the item ties it to nothing, while a heavily indebted\n    61\t  firm's cash burn changes its credit risk. The share price, a target price and other companies' figures are never conditions.\n    62\t- Link one statement to every thesis it informs, and to none that its own relevance says it does not inform; use the narrowest\n    63\t  relevant thesis only when choosing between theses that cover the same thing.\n    64\t- Match by the underlying question or outcome, subject and scope, and time when relevant, not by word overlap. A different wording,\n    65\t  source, forecast or direction alone does not make a new thesis. Related questions can be separate when their outcomes matter\n    66\t  independently.\n    67\t- Do not exclude evidence solely because it concerns a related period, population or product variant. Assess whether it can inform\n    68\t  the open question, preserving the difference in the record. Do not present a forecast for a later year as a forecast for the\n    69\t  thesis's year. If another open thesis covers the evidence more directly, consider that thesis as well; do not assume different\n    70\t  periods are automatically the same thesis or automatically unrelated.\n    71\t\n    72\tExamples of linking evidence to research:\n    73\t\n    74\t- Supply chain: an open thesis asks whether a manufacturer's production is constrained. A named supplier announces a capacity\n    75\t  expansion for a component the manufacturer uses. Link the announcement as a potential supply signal; it does not establish\n    76\t  allocations or deliveries.\n    77\t- Geopolitics: an open thesis asks whether an exporter can sell in a specified market. The relevant government proposes a licensing\n    78\t  restriction on that product. Link the proposal as evidence about market access; a proposal is not an enacted restriction.\n    79\t- Macro: an open thesis asks whether a company's borrowing costs will rise. The item reports that its floating-rate debt is tied to a\n    80\t  benchmark that has risen. Link the benchmark movement and the stated exposure; do not calculate the expense change unless the\n    81\t  source supports it.\n    82\t- Competition: an open thesis asks whether a company can retain customers in a product market. A named competitor cuts the price of a\n    83\t  competing product. Link the price cut as competitive evidence; do not assert lost customers or share without support.\n    84\t\n    85\t3. WHEN TO PROPOSE A NEW THESIS\n    86\t\n    87\tA thesis is a question a senior analyst would hold a card for: its answer could change a position because it could change the\n    88\tcompany's revenue, profit, cash or credit risk, or competitive position in a way you can name; public material will settle it on a\n    89\tdate; and no open thesis already asks it. A thesis asks one quantity for one period, or one event. It opens for one of four reasons, a closed set; a matter that fits none of them is\n    90\tevidence, kept and linked to the theses it informs or left unlinked, never a thesis:\n    91\t- product_node: when the generation of the main product that carries the company's value reaches the step that brings revenue,\n    92\t  usually first shipments; announcements and samples are its evidence, and only milestones an analyst bets on separately (a drug's\n    93\t  trial result and its approval) are separate theses (\"will the carmaker's new platform start deliveries in 2026?\";\n    94\t  \"will the drugmaker's next-generation inhaler, the product line that carries its value, reach pharmacies by mid-2027?\").\n    95\t- binding_obligation: an obligation the company takes on in its own name, large enough to change its revenue, profit, cash or credit\n    96\t  risk: guaranteeing, backing or giving credit support for another party's debt, lease, revenue or capacity, lending to it,\n    97\t  committing to buy capacity or services, or a sized stake or acquisition not yet completed. One already undertaken is tracked by its\n    98\t  amount at the next annual report; one not yet signed by whether it is signed by a check date within 18 months of the item (\"how much will the\n    99\t  utility have guaranteed for its project companies' loans at its next annual report?\"; \"will the retailer sign a guarantee for its\n   100\t  franchisees' leases, large enough to change its credit risk, by the check date?\"). Its own borrowing or leases and a completed\n   101\t  or unsized investment are not obligations.\n   102\t- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for one calendar year, this year or next (a\n   103\t  figure over a rolling twelve months or a span that is not one calendar year is not this reason's period; whether its statement is kept is judged\n   104\t  as evidence):\n   105\t  several companies' combined output or spending, a contract price, an interest rate (\"the largest container lines' combined capacity\n   106\t  added in 2026\"; \"next year's average contract price of a raw material\"). Another population or wording of the same aggregate is\n   107\t  evidence for it.\n   108\t- policy_stage: the step a policy or regulatory process reaches, naming who decides (\"will the regulator approve the drug for a second\n   109\t  indication?\"; \"will the government require licences for the product's exports by a date?\").\n   110\t\n   111\t- Open only matters an analyst would bet on separately; small matters open no thesis and their statements are kept as evidence. A\n   112\t  customer's deployment plan is evidence for the company's demand and product theses, unless it changes the company's own cash or\n   113\t  credit risk, which is judged as an obligation.\n   114\t- Give the date the item supports. When it gives none, use the date the reason fixes and say how it was set: an obligation already\n   115\t  undertaken, its next annual report; an unsigned obligation, a check date within 18 months of the item; a pending regulatory\n   116\t  decision, the current fiscal year-end. A shared quantity takes its release date and a product event the date its outcome can be\n   117\t  checked, only when the item supports one. A question no date can settle is rewritten or not opened.\n   118\t- Do not open a thesis about: an executive appointment or organisational change; the company's own borrowing or leases as an\n   119\t  obligation; a buyback authorisation or dividend declaration; a financial measure's level, growth, margin or guidance for any period,\n   120\t  on its own; an undated moat or strategy; a feature, content or software update, price point, regional service or variant of a\n   121\t  product already on sale; another estimate, source or wording of what an open thesis tracks; an annual quantity after next year (an\n   122\t  obligation excepted); shareholder votes, bylaws or routine litigation procedure. Their statements are evidence for the theses they\n   123\t  inform, or left unlinked.\n   124\t- Before proposing a new thesis, name its reason (opens_as), the public material that will settle it (settled_by), and the closest\n   125\t  open thesis with why an analyst would bet on the two separately because their answers can move apart; with no open thesis, say so.\n   126\t  If the two cannot move apart, link the evidence to every open thesis it informs instead.\n   127\t\n   128\tCounterexamples:\n   129\t\n   130\t- \"The company's outlook is interesting\" or \"the industry may change\" is too vague: it names no outcome later evidence can inform.\n   131\t- If an open thesis tracks sales growth, a revised sales forecast is evidence for it; do not open a second thesis to repeat it.\n   132\t- A customer expanding capacity informs demand; it is not a thesis of its own, and not a claim that the supplier has received orders.\n   133\t- \"Is the stock attractively valued?\" is an investment conclusion, not a research question about the business.\n   134\t\n   135\t4. HOW TO WRITE EVIDENCE\n   136\t\n   137\t- One evidence item records one statement, and that statement is what you judge: a figure, date or comparison in the neighbouring\n   138\t  words does not make another claim in the same passage new or material. A statement told in several sentences of the item, with its\n   139\t  terms, figures and conditions, is one item.\n   140\t- Write a standalone summary: who did or said what, how much and for which period, naming the measure even when a neighbouring\n   141\t  sentence gives it. Preserve conditions, uncertainty and attribution. Return every passage the summary rests on, each copied\n   142\t  verbatim and contiguously from the item, without translation; do not join distant passages with an ellipsis.\n   143\t- Name the actor in the summary and identify the original party whose action, figure or claim it is. Give the reporting speaker when\n   144\t  available. The item's publisher and publication date come from its source metadata.\n   145\t- Use only this item's information. Distinguish forecasts, allegations and unconfirmed reports from confirmed outcomes. Report plans\n     9\t- another company's matter that touches none of the company's markets (its valuation, share price, governance or a deal outside them), or that sits next to the company only by sharing an article, an event or an ecosystem; you supply the connection as the analyst and the item need not state it: a customer's spending, orders or backlog bears on demand, a supplier's capacity, output, prices or revenue on supply and input costs, a rival's products, prices or share in the company's markets on competition (\"a large customer's order backlog doubled\"; \"the main supplier's quarterly revenue jumped on demand for the part\");\n    10\t- the same fact said again in other words within this item: one deal, hire, programme or reported measure told in several sentences, with its terms, figures and growth rates, is one evidence item; keep the fuller wording (\"a $2 billion order for 120 stores in 15 countries over three years\"; \"cloud revenue of $8 billion, up 30% on the year and 6% on the quarter, 40% of the total\"); a deal one party signs under a wider programme, with its own amount or capacity, is its own evidence item, and a fact another outlet reported before is not a repeat within this item;\n    11\t- company boilerplate, bylines, forward-looking-statement text.\n    12\tA report and another party's denial or confirmation of it are two items, each kept only if it passes the test above; an estimate stays apart from any valuation drawn from it, and the valuation is not kept; one party's statement keeps its own planned or rumoured details.\n    13\tReturn only the evidence items you keep.\n    14\tThen check the theses and links. A new thesis that asks the same underlying question, about the same subject and scope, as an open thesis or another new thesis is not proposed: link its evidence to that thesis. A new thesis needs at least one kept evidence item, and a vague or noisy topic with no outcome to watch is not proposed. Each kept evidence item links to every thesis it informs and to no thesis its own relevance says it does not inform.\n    15\tFor each new thesis, check its opens_as, settled_by, closest_open_thesis and why_a_separate_bet: drop the thesis if it fits none of the four reasons in section 3, if no public material will settle it on a date, if an open thesis exists and its answer cannot move apart from it, or if it falls under a 'do not open' item in section 3; then link its evidence to every open thesis it informs, or leave it without links.\n    16\tAn item whose only home would be a new thesis that is not a big matter is returned with empty links and kept without links; an item an open thesis covers is linked there, not left without links. Then read back each statement you return with empty links that states the company's own figures: return it only if a figure can change what an analyst expects of the company's revenue, profitability, funding or credit risk, or competitive position; for example, a cash-rich company's balance or cash flow that the item ties to nothing usually cannot; return only what passes.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
